From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Melanie Riise <me@mriise.net>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:43:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [zlib][x86] Add an AVX2 VPCLMULQDQ CRC-32 kernel

VPCLMULQDQ does not require AVX-512: AMD Zen 3 and Intel client parts
without AVX-512 (Alder Lake through Meteor Lake) have it with AVX2, and
currently use the 128-bit SSE4.2 kernel. Add the AVX-512 kernel's
algorithm on 256-bit registers, selected at runtime after AVX-512 and
before SSE4.2. zlib-ng (crc32_vpclmulqdq_avx2) uses the same fold
constants and feature checks.

AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, Windows x64, clang-cl 21, GiB/s:

  bytes     SSE4.2   AVX2 (this CL)   zlib-ng AVX2
  1 KiB      17.2        31.5            26.7
  64 KiB     18.5        37.3            36.9
  16 MiB     16.5        31.8            32.4

zlib_bench gzip decompression, snappy testdata plus a 23 MiB PE, AVX2
only: +4.6% geomean (up to +16.9% on html). The zlib wrapper, which has
no CRC-32, moved +0.7%. Compression is unchanged.

Bug: TODO_FILE_CRBUG
